<title>SOUTH KOREA: Dong Won Fisheries buying back shares.</title>
<headline>Dong Won Fisheries buying back shares.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Dong Won Fisheries Co Ltd said it would buy back 200,000 common shares on the open market from January 13 to April 12 to boost the share price.  </p>
<p>The company said in a statement that it holds none of its own shares.</p>
<p>The buyback represents 10 percent of Dong Won's share capital, it said.</p>
<p>The statement said the shares would be bought at the previous day's closing price. KLB Securities and Hanwha Securities would handle the buyback.</p>
<p>Dong Won's shares closed on Thursday 100 won higher at 11,800.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
</text>
